\viewkind4\uc1\pard\fi-225\li225\sl200\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\ulnone\b0 
\par 1\cf0 .  Whenever I am healthy,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  I give thanks to the Lord;
\par  With my mouth and all my heart,
\par  I sing praises to Him.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  All the night and all the day,
\par  Thanksgiving and singing,
\par  All to Thee Oh Lord our God,
\par  For Thou preserve our lives.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  2.  My life and my energy,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  Are so precious to me
\par  All come from God's Divine Hands,
\par  Pleasant to me than gold;
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6  Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Not withstanding, no treasures
\par  Can compare with good health;
\par  But what surpasses them all
\par  Is heavenly eternal life.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par  3. And if I command respect,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0  And  I rule over them;
\par  If  I have  authority,
\par  And much wealth to boast of,
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6   Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par but, if I am not so strong.
\par   And I lay on sick bed,
\par   In  my sufferings and in pains,
\par   Am I worth anything ?
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. If by grace of the great Lord,
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 I recover fully;
\par I can see the moon and stars,
\par and brightness of the sun.
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par My eyesight becomes so clear,
\par And my ears can hear well,
\par I regain my appetite.
\par and regain my sound sleep.
\par 
\par \pard\fi-225\li225\sl190\slmult0\cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. I give  thanks to my Good Lord
\par \pard\li225\sl190\slmult0 for abundance of grace!
\par Let me glorify Thy Name,
\par and keep worshipping Thee!
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par Keep  on watch over my health!
\par the day Thou shall call me,
\par To give me eternal life.
\par \pard      And Thy heavenly rest.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b\f2\fs14 
\par }

